.TH TGLFS-INSPECT 1 "March 2026" "tglfs 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tglfs-inspect \- inspect file-card metadata and chunk references
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tglfs inspect
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIufid\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows the file-card metadata and checks whether each referenced chunk message exists and is a Telegram document. Use
.B --probe
to download, decrypt, and validate all file data. Versions 1 through 3 try the current and legacy counter pipelines. Version 4 uses the authenticated archive reader and verifies every block, the complete tar size, and its UFID without trying the older pipelines.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --no-interactive
Disable interactive prompts and fail instead of prompting.
.TP
.B --peer <peer>
Peer to inspect instead of Saved Messages.
.TP
.B --probe
Run the full integrity probe.
.TP
.B --password <password>
Password to use for the integrity probe.
.TP
.B --password-env [name]
Read the probe password from an environment variable. If no name is provided, the command uses
.B TGLFS_INSPECT_PASSWORD.
.TP
.B --password-stdin
Read the probe password from standard input.
.TP
.B --json
Emit machine-readable JSON.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TGLFS_INSPECT_PASSWORD
Default environment variable for the probe password.
